@startuml
title Service order decomposition fallout - Order fallout resolution

participant "Service Order\nManagement" as SOM #blue
participant "Event\nManagement" as Event #grey
participant "Fallout\nManagement" as FM #lightgrey
actor "Operator" as Operator
participant "Resource Catalog\nManagement" as RCM #blue

note right of FM : continued from\nchapter 5.2.1.2

FM -> FM : 1 Update fallout (state="Held")

FM -> Event : 2 **TMF688 Event Management**\nPOST event falloutStateChange\n(falloutId, state="Held")
activate Event
Event --> FM : 3 **TMF688** 201 Created
deactivate Event

group Fallout resolution assignment

    Operator -> FM : 4 Fallout resolution assignment
    Operator -> Operator : 5 Fallout manual analysis

    Operator -> RCM : 6 **TMF634 Resource Catalog Management**\nPATCH /resourceSpecification\n"msisdn characteristic valueType to String"
    activate RCM
    RCM --> Operator : 7 **TMF634** 200 OK
    deactivate RCM

    Operator -> FM : 8 Select action: continue

end

FM -> FM : 9 Update fallout\n(state="Completed", result="resolved")

FM -> Event : 10 **TMF688 Event Management**\nPOST event falloutStateChange\n(falloutId, state="Completed", result="resolved")
activate Event
Event --> FM : 11 **TMF688** 201 Created
deactivate Event

FM -> SOM : 12 **TMF641 Service Order Management**\nPATCH resourceOrder\n(resourceOrderId, resourceOrderItemId, falloutResult="resolved")
activate SOM
SOM --> FM : 13 **TMF641** 200 OK
deactivate SOM

@enduml
